 ## Subtopics
 
 ### [NeRF with Per-Image Embeddings](2484-nerf-with-per-image-embeddings.md)
-Extends MLPRender_Fea by adding a per-image embedding vector to the input, allowing the MLP to account for global appearance shifts like lighting changes across different views.
+This method extends the standard NeRF MLP architecture by learning a distinct per-image embedding vector for each scene, which is injected into the color prediction network to account for view-dependent photometric variations. It sets itself apart from standard NeRF by explicitly modeling global appearance shifts across input views, and differs from [SVS](957-unbounded-inward-facing-scene-parameterization.md) by neutralizing this variation during training to yield consistent global brightness and color across views.
 
 ### [Volume Radiance Network](2576-volume-radiance-network.md)
-A variant that may use different feature sources or MLP structures for radiance prediction.
+The Volume Radiance Network is a neural rendering module that predicts RGB color from input features, view directions, and positions using a Multi-Layer Perceptron (MLP) with positional encoding applied to features and view direction, but NOT position. It builds on [MLPRender_Fea](2414-mlprender-fea.md). Unlike [NeRF with Per-Image Embeddings](2484-nerf-with-per-image-embeddings.md) which injects global image context, or [Linear Feature Decoder with Learned Color Basis](3352-linear-feature-decoder-with-learned-color-basis.md) which uses linear projections, this method explicitly encodes view directions to model view-dependent appearance.
 
 ### [Linear Feature Decoder with Learned Color Basis](3352-linear-feature-decoder-with-learned-color-basis.md)
-Replaces the nonlinear MLP decoder with a linear decoder using a learned basis, explicitly modeling view dependence without a black-box MLP.
+This method replaces the nonlinear Multi-Layer Perceptron (MLP) decoder used in hybrid neural rendering models with a white-box linear decoder that uses spatially-localized features as coefficients for a learned basis to describe view-dependent color and density. It sets itself apart from its parent [MLPRender_Fea](2414-mlprender-fea.md) by explicitly modeling view dependence through a learned basis rather than a black-box MLP. This approach enables adaptivity for scenes with variable appearance and avoids the limited expressivity of spherical harmonic decoders.
 
 ### [Hybrid View-dependent Color Modeling](5083-hybrid-view-dependent-color-modeling.md)
-Combines a sparse feature voxel grid with a shallow MLP, separating view-independent and view-dependent components, whereas MLPRender_Fea applies PE to features and view direction but not position.
+Hybrid View-dependent Color Modeling predicts RGB color by combining a sparse feature voxel grid with a shallow Multi-Layer Perceptron (MLP). It solves the trade-off between the slow convergence of pure neural fields and the limited quality of explicit voxel grids by storing view-independent diffuse color and view-dependent features in the grid, while using the MLP to decode view-dependent residuals. It sets itself apart from [MLPRender_Fea](2414-mlprender-fea.md) by explicitly separating the view-independent component (stored in the grid) from the view-dependent component (decoded by the MLP), whereas [MLPRender_Fea](2414-mlprender-fea.md) applies positional encoding to features and view direction but not position [2414-mlprender-fea.md].
 
 ### [Color Network Architecture](7200-color-network-architecture.md)
-Defines specific layer widths and activation functions for the MLP module in dynamic view synthesis contexts.
+The Color Network Architecture is a Multi-Layer Perceptron (MLP) module used in neural rendering to predict the final RGB color of a ray at a specific 3D point, conditioned on the viewing direction and local geometric features. It solves the problem of view-dependent appearance synthesis by mapping high-dimensional input vectors to a 3D color space. It differs from its parent, [MLPRender_Fea](2414-mlprender-fea.md), by explicitly defining a three-layer fully connected structure with specific input dimensionality (position, view direction, and feature vectors) and activation functions, serving as the foundational blueprint for subsequent variants like [Neural Textures Architecture](9534-neural-textures-architecture.md) and [Decomposition Network](12532-decomposition-network.md).
 
 ### [Neural BRDF and Geometry Decoding](8139-neural-brdf-and-geometry-decoding.md)
-Decodes features into explicit BRDF values and normals, extending the color prediction to physically based rendering.
+This method decodes scene appearance features into physically plausible BRDF values, surface normals, and RGB colors using distinct Multi-Layer Perceptrons (MLPs). It extends the standard NeRF color prediction by explicitly modeling geometric properties and view-dependent reflectance, allowing for accurate relighting and normal estimation. It differs from [MLPRender_Fea](2414-mlprender-fea.md) by outputting normals and BRDF parameters in addition to color, and from [NeRF with Per-Image Embeddings](2484-nerf-with-per-image-embeddings.md) by using explicit geometric decoders rather than just per-image latent codes.
 
