-An MLP that takes encoded position, spherical harmonics encoding of view direction, normal vector, and geometric feature vector as input. It uses three layers with 128, 128, and 64 features, GELU activations, and a Sigmoid output for RGB and transparency [S8].
+Input: Encoded position, spherical harmonics encoding (degree 3) of view direction $v$, normal vector $n$ of rendered SDF, and geometric feature vector $z$ from k-SDF [S9]. Encoding: Trainable positional encoding from Rosu and Behnke [44] [S9]. MLP Structure: Three layers with 128, 128, and 64 features respectively [S9]. Activations: Hidden layers use GELU. Final layer applies Sigmoid activation to produce outputs in range [0, 1] [S9]. Output Dimensions: 3 for RGB, 1 for transparency [S9].
 
